de" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114135" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=8$ and ${\\int }_{4}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=4,$ then what is ${\\int }_{3}^{6}(5-2f(x))\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114135" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{4}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information into the above gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8+4 & ={\\int }_{3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 12 & ={\\int }_{3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the desired integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{6}(5-2f(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =5{\\int }_{3}^{6}\\text{d}x-2{\\int }_{3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\cdot x\\,{|}_{3}^{6}-2\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =5(6-3)-24 \\\\  & =5(3)-24 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114135" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0366f23d3812e03904accf1acab42f1872d82ef69e7c77814658267bfe22812" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114135" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114135" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114135" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114135" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-9"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114135" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114135" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a function such that ${\\int }_{8}^{5}3f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-2$ and ${\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-3.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{3}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{8}^{5}3f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2 \\\\ 3{\\int }_{8}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2 \\\\ -3{\\int }_{5}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2 \\\\ {\\int }_{5}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{5}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3+\\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0366f23d3812e03904accf1acab42f1872d82ef69e7c77814658267bfe22812" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d4700