"answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4795" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a  function such that ${\\int }_{2}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=8$ and ${\\int }_{2}^{0}2f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=4.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{0}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4795" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{0}2f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =4 \\\\ 2{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =4 \\\\ -2{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =4 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-2)+8 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4795" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b5d0ec2c5848b8f24d1396021f59046d97eba12d3520c179fc90f3c2667188de" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4795" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4795" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4795" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4795" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "14"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4795" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4795" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4795" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $f$ and $g$ be continuous functions such that ${\\int }_{0}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=18,{\\int }_{0}^{7}\\frac{1}{2}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x=5,$ and ${\\int }_{3}^{7}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x=4.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{7}\\frac{1}{2}\\,g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{7}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =5 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{7}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the adjacent intervals rule and substituting the known values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{7}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{7}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{7}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the sum rule for definite integrals and substituting the known values, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{7}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x+4 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{0}^{7}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x+4 \\\\ 18-10 & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x+4 \\\\ 4 & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b5d0ec2c5848b8f24d1396021f59046d97eba12d3520c179fc90f3c2667188de" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4726" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4726" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4726" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "13"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4726" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4726" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4726" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-418" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_\\pi^\\pi \\sqrt{\\sin x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/example-418.json" "file_sha256" "097303f235af4dfbf5940399479498782725edcfe25362e03a335263c8046964" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-418" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the lower and upper limits are the same. So, the integral evaluates to zero:\n\n$$\n\\int_\\pi^\\pi \\sqrt{\\sin x}\\,\\textrm d x = 0\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/example-418.json" "file_sha256" "097303f235af4dfbf5940399479498782725edcfe25362e03a335263c8046964" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-419" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{6} \\, f(x) \\; \\textrm d x = -54 },$ what is the value of\n${\\displaystyle \\int_{6}^{0} \\bigg( \\dfrac 1 3 f(x) + 1 \\bigg) \\; \\textrm d x }?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/example-419.json" "file_sha256" "fe168f882e5a059aa3206f5829677a51982f686e27d37d3d40c67f24d763e637" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-419" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{6}^{0}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{6}^{0}(\\frac{1}{3}f(x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{6}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{6}^{0}1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 54+x\\,{|}_{6}^{0} \\\\  & =18+(0-6) \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/example-419.json" "file_sha256" "fe168f882e5a059aa3206f5829677a51982f686e27d37d3d40c67f24d763e637" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-420" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $\\displaystyle \\int_7^{10}f(x)\\,\\textrm d x = 18$ and $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{7}f(x)\\,\\textrm d x = -6$ then what is $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{10} \\big( 2f(x)+1 \\big) \\,\\textrm d x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/example-420.json" "file_sha256" "aff1d27d896ae722ca35f75eac66fb135da04324c16c564bda461b495f9b7e97" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-420" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n\\int_0^{7}f(x)\\,\\textrm d x + \\displaystyle \\int_7^{10}f(x)\\,\\textrm d x = \\displaystyle \\int_0^{10}f(x)\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information into the above gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6+18={\\int }_{0}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 12={\\int }_{0}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the desired integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{10}(2f(x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{10}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(12)+x\\,{|}_{0}^{10} \\\\  & =24+(10-0) \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/example-420.json" "file_sha256" "aff1d27d896ae722ca35f75eac66fb135da04324c16c564bda461b495f9b7e97" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a  function such that ${\\displaystyle \\int_4^1 2 \\, f(x) \\, \\textrm dx = -1}$ \nand ${\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{-1} f(x) \\, \\textrm dx = 2}.$  What is the value of ${\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^4 f(x) \\, \\textrm dx}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/example-421.json" "file_sha256" "cf98b0a8b5b4b5181da2ccb5ba6bec4aa73b1a2327794f9664a5e0603683945f" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's simplify the first given integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{1}2\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-1 \\\\ 2{\\int }_{4}^{1}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-1 \\\\ -2{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-1 \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{4}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second integral can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2 \\\\ -{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2 \\\\ {\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/example-421.json" "file_sha256" "cf98b0a8b5b4b5181da2ccb5ba6bec4aa73b1a2327794f9664a5e0603683945f" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-345632" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}{cos}^{2}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2x))\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038254/state.json" "file_sha256" "e087c1d650dfa3afae76752c250cc30b9558db3bc5938fec7d7351590d655311"} {"question" "q-345632" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the lower and upper limits are the same. So, the integral evaluates to zero:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}{cos}^{2}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2x))\\,\\text{d}x=0\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038254/state.json" "file_sha256" "e087c1d650dfa3afae76752c250cc30b9558db3bc5938fec7d7351590d655311"} {"question" "q-345632" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :